.TH GIT-ALMANAC 1 "2026-08-26" "git-almanac 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
git-almanac \- render a local Git activity calendar
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git-almanac year
.RI [ repository ]
.RI [ options ]
.PP
.B git-almanac completion
.RI < bash | zsh >
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B git-almanac
reads commits reachable from one local Git ref and renders an annual activity
calendar.
It makes no network requests, needs no forge account, and does not alter Git
history or configuration.
.PP
The default interval contains 365 local calendar dates ending today, padded to
complete Sunday-through-Saturday display weeks.
Commits are grouped by author date in the local timezone.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR year " [" repository "]"
Render activity for the repository containing the current directory, or for
the supplied repository path.
.TP
.BR completion " <" bash | zsh ">"
Write a sourceable completion definition to standard output.
.SH YEAR OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --author " pattern"
Pass an author name or email pattern to Git.
.TP
.BI --path " pathspec"
Restrict history to a Git pathspec relative to the repository root.
This option may be repeated; paths containing spaces are passed without shell
interpolation.
.TP
.BI --ref " git-ref"
Select the reachable history root.
The default is HEAD.
.TP
.BI --since " YYYY-MM-DD"
Set the first counted local calendar date.
.TP
.BI --until " YYYY-MM-DD"
Set the last counted local calendar date.
The default is today.
.TP
.BI --date " author|committer"
Choose which Git timestamp is grouped into local calendar days.
The default is author.
.TP
.B --include-merges
Include merge commits.
Merges are excluded by default.
.TP
.BI --format " terminal|html|svg|json"
Select the renderer.
The default is terminal.
.TP
.BI --output " path"
Write the rendered result to a file instead of standard output.
.TP
.BI --theme " light|dark"
Select the visual palette.
The default is light.
.TP
.B --no-color
Disable ANSI colour and use distinct intensity characters.
.SH COUNTING CONTRACT
One Git log traversal reads commits reachable from the selected ref.
Each object ID is counted once.
All authors are included unless filtered, and merge commits are excluded unless
requested.
The selected author or committer timestamp is grouped in the local timezone.
A path filter uses Git pathspec semantics.
.PP
Every renderer consumes the same normalized model and deterministic four-band
intensity thresholds.
The generation timestamp is the only intentionally variable report field.
.SH OUTPUTS
Terminal output includes month and weekday labels, five intensity states,
totals, active days, the busiest day, and streaks.
When colour is disabled, distinct Unicode characters preserve intensity.
.PP
HTML is self-contained and embeds an accessible, responsive SVG.
Standalone SVG cells carry keyboard focus, accessible labels, dates, counts,
and native hover details.
JSON uses the versioned schemaVersion 1 model.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable terminal ANSI colour when the variable is present.
.TP
.B TZ
Select the process timezone through the runtime's standard timezone handling.
.TP
.B GIT_ALMANAC_INSTALL_DIR
Override the installer executable directory.
.TP
.B GIT_ALMANAC_MAN_INSTALL_DIR
Override the installer manual directory.
.TP
.B GIT_ALMANAC_VERSION
Select an exact v-prefixed release for install.sh.
.SH INSTALLATION
Install an immutable released asset with:
.nf
curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/knowledgeislands/tools-git-almanac/\
main/install.sh | bash
.fi
.PP
For local development, run:
.nf
\&./install.sh --link
git-almanac year .
.fi
.PP
Link mode requires Bun and leaves the checkout as the executable source.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Repository, Git, rendering, or output failure.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid git-almanac syntax or option value.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git (1),
.BR git-log (1)
